      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "“Often occurring in religious settings” overgeneralizes beyond the source, which describes interviews with survivors of religious conversion practices in Christian settings rather than establishing that conversion therapy commonly occurs in religious settings.",
        "The wording “described as a harmful and coercive form of spiritual abuse” is only partly supported: the source frames conversion practices as harm and says spiritual abuse is coercive, but it does not directly define conversion therapy itself as a form of spiritual abuse in general.",
        "The definition slightly compresses the source’s claim about “urgent support” into a general descriptive statement; the article argues for urgent intervention and ongoing support for survivors, but not as a broad definitional feature of conversion therapy."
      ],
